3 Splits et versionnage
Après nettoyage, le pipeline :

construit les variables finales : le libellé concaténé avec ses champs texte complémentaires, et les variables catégorielles ;
découpe les données en jeux d’entraînement, de validation et de test ;
écrit ces jeux sur S3, dans un dossier nommé d’après la date d’extraction ;
référence ce dossier, avec la liste des variables, dans un fichier de configuration partagé que lit le code d’entraînement.

Chaque entraînement logge ses jeux de données d’entrée dans MLflow : on sait donc exactement sur quel snapshot des données il a tourné.

5 Why MLOps
A model trained once and never touched again does not stay good for long, for several reasons:

the way declarants describe their activity drifts over time, as new trades, new legal forms and new phrasings appear;
business experts report errors that must be fixed quickly and permanently;
the classification itself changes: the move from NAF rev. 2 to NAF 2025 required recoding the entire training set (see Data);
the libraries the model depends on get deprecated (fastText) or move to new major versions (MLflow, PyTorch).

The rest of this note describes the system that makes this work routine: reproducible training, a versioned model registry, an API deployed through GitOps, continuous monitoring and annotation, and a retraining protocol with explicit quality gates.

The model learns from past declarations stored in the Sirene register. Each observation contains:

the activity description: free text typed by the declarant, sometimes followed by details on secondary or agricultural activity;
auxiliary variables from the declaration form:

the legal form (CJ, catégorie juridique);
the nature of the activity (NAT);
the type of form (TYP);
the surface area of the premises (SRF, grouped into bins);
whether the activity is permanent or seasonal (CRT);

the APE code that was assigned, either automatically or by a human coder.

The earliest models were trained on about 10 million declarations from the former register (2014–2022). Since the move to the new register and to NAF 2025, the training base is built from about 2.7 million recent declarations (Randriamanana and Faria 2025).






